{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: BR-10, rename tooling removed. Head 8dc9edc2bb1e46563db7848eaefe5df0e7830619, tree 4c63725c19350da8980eba200937a4bbfbe7eaa9, branch request/br10-remove-rename-tooling-20261026: four commits on the current Main 986c7120 (merge base equals Main), eight paths, all eight named by the artifacts. Review request c3bb18db, checker promise a3e8a672, request d75a32d1 (builder promise e429d3bc).\n\nRead order: the primary note at the head in full; request d75a32d1 and the tech-debt review row (notes/2026-10-25-codebase-techdebt-review.md line 585); the source diff; the generated asset; then the evidence.\n\nAcceptance (\"The three files are gone, a pointer names the commit that holds them, the Page names DAP_HOME, and node --test scripts/active-source.test.mjs passes\"): met.\n- scripts/rename-workspaces.mjs, scripts/workspace-rename-preservation.json and docs/workspace-rename.md are deleted. The pointer commit 9f5ebc81 is an ancestor of Main 986c7120, and its blob for each file equals Main's blob (1c392b0b, 0b9d7d1d, 3758492f). The sizes are 98,051, 680,364 and 3,831 bytes, which total the 782,246 the note gives.\n- The Page sentence now says \"new owner-only DAP_HOME directory\", and the existing start-ui assertion expects the same words. The CLI reads DAP_HOME first and keeps ARTROOM_HOME as an alias that must agree (packages/cli/src/config-dir.ts:32-35), so the instruction matches the CLI's behavior.\n- I ran node --test scripts/active-source.test.mjs at the head in the builder's worktree: 11 passed, and the worktree stayed clean.\n\nResidue. git grep at the head for rename-workspaces and workspace-rename finds only the dated tech-debt review note, which records the finding and should keep its text. No link, script, test or configuration refers to the removed files. The gate ran after the removal commit, so its doc-links and test steps already covered the deletion.\n\nGenerated asset. I decoded PAGE_JS at Main and at the head. Replacing the one ARTROOM_HOME with DAP_HOME in the old bundle gives the new bundle exactly. PAGE_HTML is unchanged. The new page.js SHA-256 is 47321859…, equal to the digest in the asset header.\n\nHead and gate. The one ordinary gate ran at 5ff4fc52 (tree 69d16634), after the removal, the Page change and the asset rebuild. The head differs from that checkpoint only in the note, the new delivery manifest and the removal of the unlanded owning manifest, so the documents-only rule applies and no second gate is owed. The checkpoint for the owning checks, 9414b878, differs from the gate checkpoint only in the note and that owning manifest.\n\nArchitecture: no change. The removed files had no callers. The Page change is one string, and the asset was regenerated by its own build command, not edited by hand.\n\nSecurity: no change to code paths, authority, settings or deployment. The new text names the CLI's preferred variable and keeps the instruction to use a separate owner-only directory and a key of the agent's own.\n\nSimplification: good. The head removes 20,279 lines of finished one-time tooling and leaves a single exact retrieval pointer. The evidence is more than a cleanup of this size needs (a 60-file manifest and a full callback analysis), but it is correct and costs the review nothing.\n\nEvidence, verified by me:\n- Manifest digest de2dbd1d… matches the request. All 60 files match their size and SHA-256 digest; nothing in /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-26-br10-cleanup-delivery is writable (0 of 68 entries); all 59 SHA256SUMS lines pass.\n- gate/result.json (SHA-256 614f26c8…, equal to the note) records head 5ff4fc52, tree 69d16634, Main 986c7120 before and after, exit 0, and an empty status afterwards. gate/gate.log (SHA-256 32885cd9…, equal to the note) shows changed files 0, every step at exit 0, notes 0 warnings, kernel, Node, Counting, plain 2,836 passed and 1 skipped, and native 780 passed and 2 skipped.\n- The owning checks and their digests are the